---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Your Name">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Personal Computational Laboratory</p>
    <h1>Research, notes, simulations, and technical documentation in one navigable academic website</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This site combines portfolio material, digital-garden notes, reproducible computational writing,
      software documentation, and interactive scientific laboratories with reading-first design.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card span-6">
      <h2>Research</h2>
      <p>Research themes, active directions, and scientific context.</p>
      <a href="/research/">Open research overview →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-6">
      <h2>Papers</h2>
      <p>Publications, preprints, drafts, and writing artifacts.</p>
      <a href="/papers/">Read publication area →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-4">
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <p>Software and electronics work with implementation-oriented documentation.</p>
      <a href="/projects/">Browse projects →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-4">
      <h2>Interactive Labs</h2>
      <p>Browser-based simulations for stochastic and computational systems.</p>
      <a href="/labs/">Launch laboratories →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-4">
      <h2>Quartz Notes</h2>
      <p>Interconnected digital-garden notes with backlinks and graph navigation.</p>
      <a href="/notes/">Open notes garden →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-4">
      <h2>Computational Notes</h2>
      <p>Quarto-based scientific notes with equations and executable examples.</p>
      <a href="/computational-notes/">Open computational notes →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-4">
      <h2>LaTeX Lecture Notes</h2>
      <p>PDF lecture notes with quick access for reading and reference.</p>
      <a href="/latex-notes/">Browse PDF archive →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card span-4">
      <h2>Software Docs</h2>
      <p>Documentation for scientific software and reusable research tools.</p>
      <a href="/docs/">Open docs section →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Reading-first navigation</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      The top navigation is organized by content intent: research, implementation, simulation, and references.
      Each section is scoped for quick discovery and low-friction reading.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
